# TEMPORARY FORK DEPENDENCY -- tracks Free-Ink/freeink-sdk PR #65.
#
# The pinned commit (c4906def) is upstream's own 1.6.5rc pin e30d25a0 plus one
# commit. That commit makes THREE changes, not just the hostname check:
#   1. arms wolfSSL_check_domain_name() on every non-insecure connection --
#      without it a setCACert() connection accepts any certificate signed by
#      any trusted CA for ANY hostname;
#   2. fails the connect closed when the CA buffer does not parse, instead of
#      handshaking against an empty trust store;
#   3. SecureHttpClient treats 1xx/204/304 as carrying no body (RFC 9110
#      s6.4.1). Currently latent in this firmware: runGetWolf is the only
#      SecureHttpClient path and its sole caller (OtaUpdater's pinned GitHub
#      metadata fetch) sends no If-None-Match, so no such status arrives today.
#      It removes a stall hazard -- a no-body response with no framing headers
#      would otherwise sit in readUntilClose() until the timeout -- and is a
#      prerequisite for ever re-enabling conditional GETs on that transport.
#
# That fix is submitted upstream as Free-Ink/freeink-sdk PR #65 (open). Upstream
# has no commit carrying it on an acceptable base -- the PR's own branch sits on
# an SDK older than e30d25a0 -- so the pin cannot be fetched from Free-Ink and
# CI dies at submodule checkout. This fork URL exists only to make the pin
# fetchable.
#
# REVERT to https://github.com/Free-Ink/freeink-sdk.git as soon as equivalent
# hostname verification is merged upstream onto a base at or after e30d25a0.
# Do not use this fork to carry any further divergence.
[submodule "freeink-sdk"]
	path = freeink-sdk
	url = https://github.com/sfoulad/freeink-sdk.git
	branch = main
